# the trust surface of xos, as data.
#
# docs/threat-model.md, SOURCES.md, trust/README and README.md each describe
# part of this well, in prose. nothing checked any of them against the tree --
# and the EFI stub proved what that costs: honestly described in SOURCES.md,
# and sitting next to an unpinned binary for as long as it existed.
#
# this file is the INDEX. the four documents stay the narrative and point here.
# G59 parses it and does a set-difference against the tree in six directions,
# so a new host tool, a new source, a new container package, a new blob or a
# new trust anchor cannot arrive without a row appearing beside it.
#
# fixed columns: KIND  NAME  ANCHOR  NOTE. not a markdown table -- parsing `|`
# rots. not a doc plus a machine file -- that reintroduces the drift being
# fixed.
#
#   tool    a host program the build runs. anchor: repro (its behaviour ends up
#           in the pinned bytes) or lab (signing, boot, disk, qemu only)
#   source  a pinned upstream tarball. anchor: sig:VAR (a maintainer signature
#           matched to that pinned fingerprint), urlsha512, or tofu
#   pkg     a package in the pinned container. anchor: the frozen archive day
#   blob    a prebuilt binary that enters the SIGNED image. anchor: blobs.sha256
#   host    a host path the build reads but cannot pin. a PREFIX; anything
#           under it is covered
#   img     a path inside the BUILT image, not a host input. also a prefix
#   ca      a trust anchor shipped in the image
#   out     something this build produces and pins
#kind  name                                         anchor           note

# ---- host tools --------------------------------------------------------------
tool   bc                                           repro            arch:bc -- kernel build
tool   bison                                        repro            arch:bison -- util-linux only
tool   cmake                                        repro            arch:cmake -- json-c only
tool   cmp                                          repro            arch:diffutils -- byte comparisons
tool   curl                                         repro            arch:curl -- fetches the pinned tarballs (digest+signature decide, not the url)
tool   flex                                         repro            arch:flex -- util-linux only
tool   gcc                                          repro            arch:gcc -- compiles every shipped byte -- the root of this whole table
tool   ld                                           repro            arch:binutils -- links every shipped byte
tool   lsblk                                        lab              arch:util-linux -- the mounted-disk guard reads its MOUNTPOINTS column
tool   make                                         repro            arch:make -- drives every upstream build
tool   mcopy                                        lab              arch:mtools -- writes the ESP
tool   mkfs.fat                                     lab              arch:dosfstools -- formats the ESP
tool   mksquashfs                                   repro            arch:squashfs-tools -- builds the read-only root
tool   mmd                                          lab              arch:mtools -- writes the ESP
tool   objdump                                      repro            arch:binutils -- disassembles for the G22 canary check
tool   openssl                                      repro            arch:openssl -- seals the signing keys at rest
tool   partprobe                                    lab              arch:parted -- re-reads the table after a flash
tool   patch                                        repro            arch:patch -- applies the carried patches
tool   pkg-config                                   repro            arch:pkgconf -- cryptsetup configure
tool   python3                                      repro            arch:python -- ukify and pehash.py
tool   qemu-system-x86_64                           lab              arch:qemu-base -- the selftest lab
tool   readelf                                      repro            arch:binutils -- reads ELF headers for G2/G3/G16/G22
tool   rsync                                        repro            arch:rsync -- stages the image root
tool   sbsign                                       lab              arch:sbsigntools -- signs the UKI
tool   sbverify                                     lab              arch:sbsigntools -- verifies it back
tool   sfdisk                                       lab              arch:util-linux -- writes the stick GPT
tool   strings                                      repro            arch:binutils -- reads the built busybox for G46
tool   strip                                        repro            arch:binutils -- strips the shipped binaries
tool   tar                                          repro            arch:tar -- unpacks them
tool   ukify                                        lab              arch:systemd -- wraps kernel+cmdline+stub into one PE
tool   unsquashfs                                   repro            arch:squashfs-tools -- reads it back for G12
tool   veritysetup                                  repro            arch:cryptsetup -- computes the dm-verity tree and root hash
tool   virt-fw-vars                                 lab              arch:virt-firmware -- enrolls PK/KEK/db into the qemu firmware
tool   wipefs                                       lab              arch:util-linux -- clears a stick before writing
tool   xz                                           repro            arch:xz -- kernel tarball

# ---- pinned upstream sources --------------------------------------------------
source LVM2                                         sig:LVM_FPR      libdevmapper.a only. key EXPIRED 2022-06-09 and is extended nowhere; the waiver is dated (lapses 2027-03-31) and G45 enforces it. second anchor: LVM_SHA512, fedora rawhide's digest for the identical tarball
source abduco                                       tofu             session detach. no upstream signature
source bearssl                                      tofu             tls for tlstunnel. no upstream signature
source busybox                                      sig:BB_FPR       the entire userland bar EXTRA_BINS
source cryptsetup                                   sig:CS_FPR       p3 luks
source dropbear                                     sig:DB_FPR       the one listening service
source ii                                           tofu             irc client. suckless publishes no signature -- trust-on-first-use over tls
source json-c                                       tofu             cryptsetup dependency. github tag tarball, no signature
source linux                                        sig:LNX_FPR      the kernel
source popt                                         urlsha512        the fedora lookaside url names the sha512, so the host cannot serve anything else there
source util-linux                                   sig:UTL_FPR      libuuid/libblkid for cryptsetup
source wireguard-tools                              tofu             configures the in-kernel wireguard. no per-release signature

# ---- packages in the pinned container -----------------------------------------
pkg    bc                                           ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    binutils                                     ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    bison                                        ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    cmake                                        ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    cryptsetup                                   ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    curl                                         ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    diffutils                                    ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    flex                                         ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    gcc                                          ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    git                                          ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    gnupg                                        ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    make                                         ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    musl                                         ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    openssl                                      ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    patch                                        ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    pkgconf                                      ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    python                                       ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    rsync                                        ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    squashfs-tools                               ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    tar                                          ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    which                                        ala:2026/09/12   
pkg    xz                                           ala:2026/09/12   

# ---- prebuilt binaries inside the signed image --------------------------------
blob   /usr/lib/systemd/boot/efi/linuxx64.efi.stub  blobs.sha256     the systemd EFI stub. runs before dm-verity covers anything

# ---- host paths the build reads -----------------------------------------------
host   /usr/lib/musl/                               UNPINNED         the libc every shipped binary statically links. see "the frontier"
host   /usr/share/edk2/                             lab              qemu secure-boot firmware. never shipped, never in a pinned byte
host   /usr/share/OVMF/                             lab              the same, laid out debian-style
host   /usr/share/qemu/                             lab              the same again

# ---- paths inside the built image, not host inputs ----------------------------
img    /usr/local                                   -                the prefix upstream configures install into
img    /usr/share/learn                             -                the learn corpus, shipped in the squashfs
img    /usr/share/xos                               -                the fingerprint wordlist
img    /usr/share/udhcpc                            -                the dhcp hook script

# ---- trust anchors shipped in the image ---------------------------------------
ca     isrg-root-x1.pem                             tofu             the only CA tlstunnel will accept. see trust/README

# ---- what this build produces ------------------------------------------------
out    xos.img                                      image.sha256     the verity-backed root image
out    rootfs.squashfs                              image.sha256     the read-only root
out    verity.roothash                              image.sha256     goes into the SIGNED cmdline
out    bzImage                                      image.sha256     the kernel
out    xos-signed.efi                               keys/db          the UKI. signed with the secure-boot db key, not pinned -- it carries a signature
out    attest/NNNN.manifest                         RELEASE_FPRS     the release claim. signed, chained, see docs/attestation.md

# ---- the frontier ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# gcc is the root of this table and nothing below changes that. a compiler that
# lies backdoors everything above it, and no row here detects that.
#
# diverse double-compilation (Wheeler): SCOPED AND REJECTED. naive cross-distro
# byte-comparison is not DDC and cannot work -- a different gcc/binutils/musl
# produces different bytes every time, which is exactly why G13 SKIPs off its
# pinned toolchain. real DDC compiles gcc's own source with a second compiler,
# rebuilds gcc with the result, and compares against the suspect compiler's
# self-build. it needs gcc built from source twice, gcc's own build made
# bit-reproducible (a research project), 8-16 GB of RAM this hardware does not
# have, 10-20 machine-hours per run, and a re-run on every gcc bump. calling
# anything cheaper "DDC" would be the overselling SOURCES.md exists to avoid.
# (gcc's own stage2-vs-stage3 `make bootstrap` comparison is NOT DDC: a
# trojaned stage1 propagates into both.)
#
# worth recording: arsenal/build-arsenal-c.sh already builds in Alpine -- a
# second, independently OPERATED toolchain. not independently ROOTED: Alpine,
# Arch, Debian and Fedora all bootstrap from a previous binary of themselves,
# and there is no independently-rooted x86-64 C compiler outside the
# Guix/live-bootstrap lineage. comparing two detects a compromise at one
# distro's build farm, not a Thompson attack in the shared ancestry.
#
# full-source bootstrap (hex0 -> tcc -> gcc): SCOPED AND REJECTED, documented
# rather than built. ~250 sequential steps, 10-20 machine-hours per run, 8-16 GB
# for the upper gcc stages, and 2-4 person-months merely to CONSUME an existing
# bootstrap. the ongoing cost is worse than the one-time cost: every gcc bump
# re-runs the chain or the claim goes stale, and a 15-hour gate blocking a
# CVE-driven re-pin loses that fight every time. docs/threat-model.md already
# puts this adversary below its defend line, and its own four-question test
# answers this one no. see live-bootstrap and bootstrappable.org. no gate: a
# gate for something you are not doing is decoration.
#
# building the EFI stub from systemd source: SCOPED AND REJECTED. it trades one
# digest-pinned 134 KB blob for meson, ninja, jinja, the systemd tree and three
# new unpinned host deps -- the opposite of shrinking this table.
#
# deleting the stub and using the kernel's own EFI stub: SCOPED AND REJECTED,
# and this one is not close. systemd-stub refuses a firmware-supplied cmdline
# under SecureBoot; the kernel stub does not -- it parses initrd= and nokaslr
# out of LoadOptions first, and CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y means anyone who can
# write a BootXXXX NVRAM entry could attach an unsigned initrd.
